## 1. What This Project Is

<PROJECT_NAME> is <WHAT IT DOES>. It is released under the <LICENSE> license and is developed in the open — anyone may read the source, file issues, propose changes, or fork it.

Because the project is open source, contributions arrive from many different environments and toolchains. This document therefore specifies **exactly one canonical setup path** so that builds are reproducible for everyone, regardless of which editor or AI assistant a given contributor prefers.

**Design goals**

| Goal | How it is enforced |
|---|---|
| Reproducible installs | Fully pinned `requirements.txt` + hash-checked lock file |
| Consistent formatting | `ruff` + `black`, run via pre-commit |
| Predictable reviews | PR template, conventional commits, required CI |
| Tool-neutral contribution | No contributor is required to use any specific AI tool |

