## 3. Quick Start (5 Minutes)

```bash
# 1. Fork on GitHub, then clone YOUR fork
git clone https://github.com/<YOUR_USERNAME>/<REPO>.git
cd <REPO>

# 2. Add the upstream remote so you can stay in sync
git remote add upstream https://github.com/<ORG>/<REPO>.git

# 3. Create an isolated environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # macOS / Linux
# .venv\Scripts\activate         # Windows PowerShell

# 4. Upgrade the installer itself, then install PINNED dependencies
python -m pip install --upgrade pip==<PINNED_PIP_VERSION>
pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt

# 5. Install the package in editable mode with dev extras
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# 6. Install git hooks
pre-commit install

# 7. Verify everything works
pytest -q
```

If step 7 passes, you are ready to work. Nothing else is required.

